      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it would be better to change these macro names to something like:\n\nIT8801_KEYBOARD_PWM_I2C_PORT\nIT8801_KEYBOARD_PWM_I2C_ADDR_FLAGS\n\nAnd document that these values are only used when accessing the keyboard and PWM function of the IT8801 chip.  I/O expander functions are accessed using the ioex_config[] array.  A board could in theory have two IT8801 chips, one used for keyboard+PWM+GPIO, and a second used for GPIO only.\n\nA more involved change would be to break this driver into multiple files, but that is out of scope at the moment.",
